\ A generated struct field getter made polymorphic by a field-name collision
\ with the always-loaded prelude, dispatched under AOT. The prelude's
\ `constraint-info` record carries an `id` field, so defining a user struct with
\ the same field name gives the `id>>` generic two methods: the prelude's
\ accessor and this struct's. A polymorphic getter routes through the dispatch
\ helper rather than devirtualizing, so it depends on the method dispatch
\ entries replaying across the freeze->runtime boundary. Without that replay the
\ `id>>` call on a `thing` instance misses and raises, so a correct printed
\ value proves the replayed method dispatched.

thing: struct{ id } ;

5 make-thing id>> .
